Subject: cmd/internal/obj/wasm: add the threads proposal's instructions
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

The assembler gains the threads proposal's instructions: memory.atomic
wait and notify, atomic.fence, and the atomic loads, stores,
read-modify-writes and compare-exchanges of every width, encoded with
the 0xFE prefix, the natural alignment of the access and the constant
offset the instruction was given. Assembly files built for an engine
that has them can use them. wasi_thread_start joins the entry functions
assembled without the Go prologue and without the PC_B parameter, since
the WASIX runtime calls it with its own two arguments.

